/E (dd dd is a command-line tool widely used in Unix-based environments that allows for raw disk cloning. dd is often used in incident response scenarios due to its lightweight nature and ability to perform raw cloning at scale. However, it comes with fewer safeguards compared to more specialized tools like FTK Imager.)
