/T (WinPMEM As the name suggests, WinPMEM is a widely used tool for acquiring live memory on Windows systems. As with all memory capture tools, it creates a memory dump file, which can be analyzed later to identify artifacts related to processes, network activity, and other evidence, all of which are handy when building an attack timeline.)
/E (WinPMEM As the name suggests, WinPMEM is a widely used tool for acquiring live memory on Windows systems. As with all memory capture tools, it creates a memory dump file, which can be analyzed later to identify artifacts related to processes, network activity, and other evidence, all of which are handy when building an attack timeline.)
